    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
    )
}

html_export_graph_page {
    Html export should provide an interactive graph page with search, filters, and links back into idea and cluster pages.
    The graph should support scoped views for workspace, file, cluster, and idea contexts.
    The workspace graph page must include every idea in the export scope — blocks, oneliners, and ideasets — and must not apply the interactive Ideas Summary GRAPH_MAX_NODES budget.
    Ideasets are visible by default with a Hide ideasets / Show ideasets toggle, matching the external-file visibility control
    (explicit AST ideasets only — distinct from hosting-file treatment).
    Hosting `.rq` files (implicit ideasets) use a Files `<select>` — hidden / compound / linked —
    with option tooltips, per ["../extension/workspace-summary/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".file_treatment_toggle]
    (parity with Ideas Summary). Compound mode draws hittable/draggable bounding boxes with clickable titles;
    linked mode adds synthetic ideaset nodes that navigate via `hostFilePageUrl` / `pageUrl`.
    Wildcard fan-out edges (`wildcard_reference`) are visible by default with a "Wildcard refs" chip
    (same label/default as Ideas Summary); turning it off client-filters those edges and draws them dotted when on —
    see ["../extension/workspace-summary/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".wildcard_refs_toggle] and
    ["../extension/workspace-summary/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".webview_export_graph_parity].
    Status and tag filters are multi-select and distinguish [graph_status_tag_filters].
    Per-idea, per-file, and per-cluster neighbourhood graphs may still use a capped budget for focused pages.
    [html_export_graph_links]
    [html_export_graph_layout]
    [html_export_graph_animation]
    [html_export_graph_background_load]
    [html_export_graph_subject]
    [html_export_graph_labels]
    [html_export_graph_label_modes]
    [html_export_graph_label_auto]
    [html_export_graph_interaction]
    [html_export_graph_metadata]
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/snapshot.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/app.js"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/src/api.rs"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:workspace_graph_includes_every_idea_when_max_graph_nodes_is_below_count"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_workspace_graph_includes_wildcard_refs_chip_and_edges"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/tests/export.rs:html_export_honours_graph_page_url_base_and_header_link"]
    )
}

html_export_graph_links {
    Graph node hrefs must resolve to idea pages from every export page depth, including nested idea, file, and cluster pages.
    Node urls should be export-root-relative so path segments such as ideas/ are not dropped when resolving from nested pages.
    When [html_export_url_base] is set, runtime resolution of those urls must honour the mount prefix (same contract as page and asset hrefs).
    External file nodes should resolve to [html_export_file_pages] or [html_export_code_reference_pages] when those page families are enabled.
    Hosting-file linked nodes (["../extension/workspace-summary/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".file_treatment_toggle] linked mode) prefer `hostFilePageUrl` stamped during graph URL enrichment
    (file / code-file page for the idea's `fileUri`), falling back to a member idea `pageUrl` when file pages are disabled.
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_utils.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/app.js"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:url_base_and_header_link_produce_root_relative_hrefs"]
    )
}

html_export_graph_layout {
    The interactive export graph should lay out nodes so labels and circles do not heavily overlap.
    Initial placement should settle with the same Obsidian-style force model as [layout_physics] (central gravity, edge springs, inverse-square repulsion).
    Rendering uses canvas 2d (not SVG DOM) with shared physics from ["../../packages/extension/webviews/shared/graph/physics-core.js"], inlined into the export asset ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/app.js"].
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/app.js"]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/shared/graph/physics-core.js"]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/shared/graph/graph-physics.ts"]
    )
}

html_export_graph_animation {
    Live physics in the HTML export should match Ideas Summary animatePhysics: continuous damped semi-implicit Euler using the defaults from ["../../packages/extension/webviews/shared/graph/physics-core.js"] (same module as ["../../packages/extension/webviews/shared/graph/graph-physics.ts"]), inlined in ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/app.js"].
    A Live physics toggle pauses and resumes the same simulation state (default off); when off, the graph batch-settles then sleeps.
    Batch settle must remain responsive per [html_export_graph_background_load] — yield between chunks rather than freezing the page for large graphs.
    Simulation should converge and sleep when calm, waking on filter changes or when Live physics is turned back on, aligned with [layout_physics].
    Large graphs use a spatial grid + repulsion cutoff in the shared core; all nodes and full labels remain visible.
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/app.js"]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/shared/graph/physics-core.js"]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/shared/graph/graph-physics.ts"]
    )
}

html_export_graph_background_load {
    Interactive HTML export graph boot and layout settle must not monopolise the main thread on large graphs.
    Page chrome (nav, filters, search, other controls) should stay responsive while the graph initialises.
    Graph wiring should start after the first paint / idle opportunity rather than synchronously blocking `DOMContentLoaded`.
    When Live physics is off, the initial batch settle should run in yielded chunks (animation frames or idle callbacks) so the browser can paint and handle input between steps; keep the boot spinner until the first usable canvas frame, then show progressive settle status.
    A new filter/refresh or remount must cancel any in-flight background settle before starting another.
    Cross-refs [html_export_graph_page], [html_export_graph_animation], [html_export_graph_interaction].
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/app.js"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
    )
}

html_export_graph_subject {
    When a graph view has a subject or center idea, that node should be visually distinct from peers and externals.
    Subject styling should use the brand rust accent against cyan peer nodes.
    @implementation (
