html_export_graph_label_auto {
    Export-surface wiring for [graph_label_auto]: canvas paint applies continuous zoom opacity (GRAPH_LABEL_FADE_START → GRAPH_LABEL_FADE_END); hover/drag stays fully opaque.
    Labels stay fully invisible while the graph is initialising or batch-settling so text paint does not lag those phases; zoom fade applies only after settle completes.
    Zoom and Fit from [html_export_graph_interaction] / [manual_reframe] update opacity each paint.
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/app.js"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
    )
}

html_export_graph_interaction {
    The interactive export graph should support dragging nodes and panning or zooming the viewport, aligned with [view_controls] and [manual_reframe].
    Click-through to idea pages must remain available after drag via click-versus-drag discrimination.
    A Fit control should reframe the viewport to the current node set without restarting layout or clearing live physics state.
    Zoom and Fit must continuously drive [graph_label_auto] / [html_export_graph_label_auto] opacity when Labels is in auto mode.
    When ["../extension/workspace-summary/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".file_treatment_toggle] is compound: file bounding boxes are hittable — drag moves member nodes together;
    clicking the underlined title navigates to the hosting file page (when `hostFilePageUrl` / `pageUrl` is present).
    When linked: synthetic file ideaset nodes are dragged and clicked like other leaves.
    Related: ["../extension/workspace-summary/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".file_treatment_toggle],
    ["../extension/workspace-summary/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".webview_export_graph_parity].
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/app.js"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
    )
}

html_export_graph_metadata {
    Graph nodes in the HTML export should surface tags, status, and attribute keys on or beside the node, not only as filter inputs.
    Attribute values declared on the idea should be reachable from the graph via the idea page and on-node attribute key summary.
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/app.js"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/snapshot.rs"]
    )
}

html_export_printable_pages {
    Html export should provide static printable pages alongside the interactive site.
    Print pages should not depend on the interactive javascript bundle.
    Status and tags are nullable: when absent, printable sheets must omit those fields rather than inventing placeholders such as unspecified or empty dashes.
    When print pages are browsed in interactive runtime mode, long lists with content below them follow [html_export_scrollable_lists].
    Idea cards on the printable report follow [html_export_print_idea_cards], [html_export_print_in_page_anchors], [html_export_print_all_attributes], and [html_export_print_button].
    Stored idea body spaces on print pages follow [html_export_print_body_whitespace].
    Ordering of cards on the printable report is tracked by [html_export_print_order_by].
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_utils.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/styles.css"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html.rs"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
    )
}

html_export_print_idea_cards {
    The printable report page lists ideas as cards in a single column that must remain within the page width on narrow viewports — no horizontal spill from long summaries, file paths, refs, or attribute values.
    Cards use a one-column grid (`minmax(0, 1fr)`) and wrapping/overflow rules so content reflows instead of overflowing the layout.
    Stored idea body spaces on these cards follow [html_export_print_body_whitespace].
    Cross-refs [html_export_printable_pages], [html_export_print_in_page_anchors], [html_export_print_all_attributes].
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/styles.css"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
    )
}

html_export_print_body_whitespace {
    The printable report must show the idea body text that the parser stores.
    Each per-idea printable sheet must show the stored idea body text.
    The parser removes the base indent.
    The base indent is the indent of the first body line.
    Extra indent on a later line is part of the body text.
    A later line with 4 more spaces than the first body line is stored with those 4 spaces.
    Print HTML must keep those leading spaces.
    Print HTML must not collapse those spaces.
    The body text must still wrap inside the card width.
    Cross-refs [html_export_printable_pages], [html_export_print_idea_cards].
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/styles.css"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:print_pages_keep_relative_body_indent"]
    )
}

html_export_print_in_page_anchors {
    On the printable report page, each idea card has a stable html `id` derived from the idea identity.
    Cross-idea links rendered on that page (title links and inline idea refs in summaries/attributes) must resolve to same-page `#` fragment urls targeting those ids, not separate idea detail pages.
    When browsed with the sticky site topbar, fragment navigation must leave the target card fully visible below the header (scroll padding / scroll-margin), not clipped behind it.
    Aligns with stable in-page anchors in [html_export_internal_links].
    Cross-refs [html_export_printable_pages], [html_export_print_idea_cards].
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_utils.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/styles.css"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
    )
}

html_export_print_all_attributes {
    Printable report idea cards and per-idea printable sheets must show every declared attribute for the idea, not only status (or status+tags).
    Attribute values that contain idea refs follow the link rules of the hosting print surface ([html_export_print_in_page_anchors] on the report page).
    Cross-refs [html_export_printable_pages], [html_export_idea_pages].
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_utils.rs"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
    )
}

html_export_print_button {
    Printable report and printable idea sheets include a Print control that opens the browser print dialog (`window.print`).
    The control must work without the interactive javascript bundle (inline handler is acceptable) and should be hidden in the printed output.
    Cross-refs [html_export_printable_pages].
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/styles.css"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
    )
}

html_export_print_order_by {
    The printable report should support ordering idea cards by a chosen field or attribute (for example name, status, file path, or a custom attribute key).
    Consumers should be able to select or configure the sort so printed documents follow a deliberate sequence rather than only the default export order.
    Not implemented yet — tracked for a follow-up.
    Cross-refs [html_export_printable_pages], [html_export_print_idea_cards].
    @status todo
}

html_export_runtime_modes {
    Html export should support a richer interactive site mode and a leaner document or print-oriented mode from the same export manifest.
    Template identifiers should select real rendering behavior rather than metadata only.
    Scrollable list viewports from [html_export_scrollable_lists] apply only in interactive mode; document and print modes keep full-length lists.
}

html_export_scrollable_lists {
    In interactive runtime mode, long list and table sections that have additional content below them should render inside a scrollable viewport with a max height so lower sections remain reachable without endless page scrolling.
    Toolbar titles and filters for those sections should stay outside the scroll viewport.
    In document and print runtime modes, those same lists should expand to their full natural height so the export remains readable as a continuous document and suitable for printing.
    Browser print of interactive pages should also expand constrained lists to full height.
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/styles.css"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
    )
}

html_export_header_link {
    Html export should accept an optional header link (href + label) rendered in the topbar ahead of section navigation.
    Hosts such as the marketing site build can set this so readers can return to the parent site from any exported page.
    When omitted, the topbar shows only the export section nav.
    Site embed consumption: ["../site/site.rq".spec_html_export].
    Often paired with [html_export_url_base] when the export is mounted under a parent static site.
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/types.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/snapshot.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/assets/styles.css"]
        ["../../packages/cli/src/commands/export.ts"]
        ["../../site/scripts/export-spec.mts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:url_base_and_header_link_produce_root_relative_hrefs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/tests/export.rs:html_export_honours_graph_page_url_base_and_header_link"]
    )
}

html_export_url_base {
    Html export should accept an optional urlBase mount prefix (for example `/spec` or `/reqlan/spec`).
    When set, page and asset hrefs must be root-relative under that prefix so static hosts resolve correctly whether the directory URL includes a trailing slash.
    When omitted, exports keep document-relative hrefs suitable for local folder browsing.
    Applies across [html_export_internal_links] and [html_export_graph_links]; site embed consumption: ["../site/site.rq".spec_html_export].
    Often paired with [html_export_header_link] when the export is mounted under a parent static site.
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/types.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_utils.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/snapshot.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/src/html_template/mod.rs"]
        ["../../packages/cli/src/commands/export.ts"]
        ["../../site/scripts/export-spec.mts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:url_base_and_header_link_produce_root_relative_hrefs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/tests/export.rs:html_export_honours_graph_page_url_base_and_header_link"]
    )
}
